REGENT OF LABUHANBATU SELATAN

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE.

Article 2

Protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect for Human Rights;
b. the right to life, survival, and development;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of the Child;
e. justice and Gender equality; and
f. victim protection.

Article 23

Forms of P2TP2A Services include:
a. Medical services, in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of Victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. Psychosocial services are services provided in order to restore the traumatic condition of Victims, including the provision of Safe Houses to protect Victims from various threats and intimidation for Victims and provide social support so that Victims have self-confidence, strength and independence, in resolving their problems;
c. Medico-legal services are forms of medical services for the purposes of evidence in the legal field;
d. Legal services to assist Victims in undergoing legal processes; and
e. Economic independence services in the form of skills training and providing economic access so that Victims can be independent.

Article 40

1. The Regent coordinates the protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence with:
a. the government;
b. regency/city regional governments;
c. vertical agencies;
d. educational institutions; and
e. community institutions.
2. Coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. religious affairs;
b. health affairs;
c. education affairs;
d. social affairs;
e. legal affairs;
f. labor affairs; and
g. other affairs.
3. Coordination as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their authority.

Article 10

Neglect as referred to in Article 6 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a Child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a Child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the scope of their Household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the Victim is under the control of that person.

Article 27

1. The Regional Government through the regional apparatus in charge of Women and Children is obliged to compile data and information regarding the protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence.
2. Data and information as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. Women and Children who are Victims of acts of Violence;
b. fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children;
c. Women and Children at risk or vulnerable; and
d. Women and Children who require special protection.
3. In managing data and information on Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (2), it is obligatory to:
a. compile a data and information system;
b. create disaggregated data;
c. conduct studies on the development of problems of Women and Children against acts of Violence; and
d. conduct periodic publication of data and information that is publicly accessible.
4. As material for the completeness of data and information as referred to in paragraph (3), the regional apparatus in charge of the protection of Women and Children cooperates and requests data from related agencies.

Article 4

This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. respect and protect Human Rights;
b. guarantee the rights of every Woman and Child to survival, growth and development;
c. non-discrimination;
d. protect Women and Children from threats, fear, torture and or treatment that degrades the degree, self-esteem and dignity of humanity;
e. prevent forms of violence against Women and Children;
f. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against Women and Children;
g. protect and provide a sense of security for Women and Children;
h. provide services to Women and Children victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
i. protect and prevent all forms of discrimination against Women and Children in the region;
j. Women's Empowerment;
k. the best interests of the Child; and
l. realize a region that is suitable for Women and Children.

Article 22

1. Prevention of Violence against Women and Children as referred to in Article 21, is implemented by regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. Women's empowerment and Child Protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and
g. peace and order.
2. Prevention of Violence by regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the regional action plan.
3. Further provisions regarding the mechanism for implementing prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

