d. rehabilitation, Repatriation and Social Reintegration.

Article 28

1. Data and information as referred to in Article 27 become material for the formulation of policies, programs, budgets, monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence.
2. The formulation of policies, programs, budgets, monitoring and evaluation as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented with the mechanism of:
a. making mapping, long-term, medium-term and short-term plans;
b. making agreements on the periodization of monthly and annual work meetings;
c. making agreements on the collection, mapping and presentation of data between regional apparatus organizations;
d. incorporating agreements into programs and budgets; and
e. conducting scheduling of monitoring, evaluation and reporting.

Article 26

1. Forms of Services provided to Women and Children Victims of Violence, are as follows:
a. Complaint services;
b. Health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medico-legal;
f. Identification services; and
g. Psychological services.
2. Forms of Services as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. Women's empowerment and Child protection; and
d. mental and spiritual.
3. In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (2), the regional government cooperates with government agencies, provincial government, other district/city governments, the Community, Families and parents.
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures for Services, and handling of Women and Children Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraphs (1), (2), and (3), are regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 5

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. forms of Violence;
b. rights of Victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
e. coordination and cooperation;
f. Community and business participation;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. reporting; and
i. sources of funds.

Article 16

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Community as referred to in Article 13 letter b, are implemented in the form of Community participation.
2. Forms of Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
a. forming family partners at the Village/Sub-district level;
b. forming women and child protection units within community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of the rights of Women and Children;
d. providing first aid to Victims; and
e. reporting to the competent authority if Violence against Victims occurs in their environment.
3. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by individuals, social community institutions, community self-help institutions, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.
4. Forms of Community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), are carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 21

The Regional Government conducts prevention of acts of Violence against Women and Children, through:
a. socialization activities of laws and regulations to the Community related to the protection of the rights of Women and Children;
b. conducting empowerment and awareness to Families, parents and the Community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling. c. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
d. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social Services;
e. opening employment opportunities for Women;
f. building community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
g. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
h. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various community non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about Women and Children;
i. opening complaint posts for the protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence; and
j. training of P2TP2A members related to the implementation of their duties in preventing Violence against Women and Children.

Article 4

This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. respect and protect Human Rights;
b. guarantee the rights of every Woman and Child to survival, growth and development;
c. non-discrimination;
d. protect Women and Children from threats, fear, torture and or treatment that degrades the degree, self-esteem and dignity of humanity;
e. prevent forms of violence against Women and Children;
f. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against Women and Children;
g. protect and provide a sense of security for Women and Children;
h. provide services to Women and Children victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
i. protect and prevent all forms of discrimination against Women and Children in the region;
j. Women's Empowerment;
k. the best interests of the Child; and
l. realize a region that is suitable for Women and Children.

Article 27

1. The Regional Government through the regional apparatus in charge of Women and Children is obliged to compile data and information regarding the protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence.
2. Data and information as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. Women and Children who are Victims of acts of Violence;
b. fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children;
c. Women and Children at risk or vulnerable; and
d. Women and Children who require special protection.
3. In managing data and information on Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (2), it is obligatory to:
a. compile a data and information system;
b. create disaggregated data;
c. conduct studies on the development of problems of Women and Children against acts of Violence; and
d. conduct periodic publication of data and information that is publicly accessible.
4. As material for the completeness of data and information as referred to in paragraph (3), the regional apparatus in charge of the protection of Women and Children cooperates and requests data from related agencies.

Article 22

1. Prevention of Violence against Women and Children as referred to in Article 21, is implemented by regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. Women's empowerment and Child Protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and
g. peace and order.
2. Prevention of Violence by regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the regional action plan.
3. Further provisions regarding the mechanism for implementing prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

REGIONAL REGULATION OF LABUHANBATU SELATAN REGENCY

NUMBER 7 OF 2023

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF LABUHANBATU SELATAN,

Considering:

a. that violence against women and children in Labuhanbatu Selatan Regency continues to increase, causing community members to feel unsafe in carrying out their lives, thus requiring integrated protection efforts;
