CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 12

Every Victim has the right to receive:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. health services in accordance with medical needs;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. special handling related to the confidentiality of the Victim;
f. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
g. guarantees of rights related to status as a Family member or Community member; and
h. spiritual guidance services.

CHAPTER II

FORMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 6

Forms of Violence against Women and Children may include:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect; and
e. exploitation.

Article 5

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. forms of Violence;
b. rights of Victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
e. coordination and cooperation;
f. Community and business participation;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. reporting; and
i. sources of funds.

Article 38

The forms of behavioral change that can be implemented to carry out Child Protection as referred to in Article 37 paragraph (2) include:
a. developing Children according to their abilities, talents, and interests;
b. preventing marriage at child age;
c. caring for, maintaining, educating and protecting Children;
d. preventing brawls between students;
e. providing opportunities for mothers to provide exclusive breastfeeding for Children;
f. instilling noble character and respect for parents;
g. instilling cultural identity, local language, love for the environment; and
h. providing special protection to Children in emergency situations, Children in conflict with the law, Children from minority and isolated groups, Children exploited economically and/or sexually, Children who are trafficked, Children who are Victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic, and other addictive substance abuse (drugs), Children Victims of kidnapping, sale and trafficking, Children Victims of Violence both physical and/or mental, Children with disabilities, and Children Victims of maltreatment and neglect, Children Victims of HIV/AIDS transmission and Children Victims of social conflict.

Article 26

1. Forms of Services provided to Women and Children Victims of Violence, are as follows:
a. Complaint services;
b. Health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medico-legal;
f. Identification services; and
g. Psychological services.
2. Forms of Services as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. Women's empowerment and Child protection; and
d. mental and spiritual.
3. In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (2), the regional government cooperates with government agencies, provincial government, other district/city governments, the Community, Families and parents.
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures for Services, and handling of Women and Children Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraphs (1), (2), and (3), are regulated by Regent Regulation.

