CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 12

Every Victim has the right to receive:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. health services in accordance with medical needs;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. special handling related to the confidentiality of the Victim;
f. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
g. guarantees of rights related to status as a Family member or Community member; and
h. spiritual guidance services.

Article 27

1. The Regional Government through the regional apparatus in charge of Women and Children is obliged to compile data and information regarding the protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence.
2. Data and information as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. Women and Children who are Victims of acts of Violence;
b. fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children;
c. Women and Children at risk or vulnerable; and
d. Women and Children who require special protection.
3. In managing data and information on Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (2), it is obligatory to:
a. compile a data and information system;
b. create disaggregated data;
c. conduct studies on the development of problems of Women and Children against acts of Violence; and
d. conduct periodic publication of data and information that is publicly accessible.
4. As material for the completeness of data and information as referred to in paragraph (3), the regional apparatus in charge of the protection of Women and Children cooperates and requests data from related agencies.

Article 40

1. The Regent coordinates the protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence with:
a. the government;
b. regency/city regional governments;
c. vertical agencies;
d. educational institutions; and
e. community institutions.
2. Coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. religious affairs;
b. health affairs;
c. education affairs;
d. social affairs;
e. legal affairs;
f. labor affairs; and
g. other affairs.
3. Coordination as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their authority.

Article 33

To implement the protection of Women and Children, the Regional Government conducts Gender Mainstreaming which includes:
a. providing references for regional apparatus in formulating Gender integration strategies carried out through planning, formulation, implementation, budgeting, monitoring and evaluation of development policies, programs and activities.
b. developing Gender-based information systems;
c. facilitating institutional strengthening and development of Gender Mainstreaming mechanisms in government institutions, women's study centers, research and development institutions, and non-governmental institutions;
d. implementing development, education, health, economy, law, Human Rights and politics, environment and social affairs that take into account Gender aspects and are child-friendly;
e. providing protection for Women especially protection for Victims of Violence, female workers, Women Victims of trafficking in persons, elderly Women, and Women with disabilities, and disaster-affected areas; and
f. facilitating the strengthening and development of networks of community institutions or organizations and the business world for the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming.

Article 2

Protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect for Human Rights;
b. the right to life, survival, and development;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of the Child;
e. justice and Gender equality; and
f. victim protection.

Article 19

1. P2TP2A as referred to in Article 18 consists of elements of the Community, universities, professional organizations, community organizations concerned with the Community.
2. The establishment of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) is stipulated by Regent's decree.
3. The implementation of Services to Victims is carried out in an integrated manner by Village/Sub-district P2TP2A, District P2TP2A, and Regency P2TP2A.
4. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the duty to:
a. receive complaints/reports of Violence against Women and/or Children, consultation, and counseling;
b. receive and send to other Service units in a tiered manner;
c. provide legal assistance;
d. health;
e. Social Rehabilitation;
f. legal Services;
g. repatriation and social reintegration; and
h. provide protection to Victims, reporters and witnesses.
5. P2TP2A may provide temporary services and protection in the form of a Safe House.
6. In the event that P2TP2A does not yet have a Safe House as referred to in paragraph (5), then Victims of Violence are referred to P2TP2A that has a Safe House.
7. P2TP2A consists of several Divisions consisting of:
a. Complaint Service division;
b. health Service division;
c. legal aid consultation; and
d. rehabilitation, Repatriation and Social Reintegration.

Article 32

1. Fulfillment of social welfare of Women and Children for prevention as referred to in Article 31 paragraph (1) includes:
a. enhancement of the Regional Government's role in the protection of Children including Children with special needs, Children with disabilities and other vulnerable Children;
b. raising Community awareness including Children regarding the protection and participation of Women and Children;
c. capacity building of the Community, Family, including Children and social welfare institutions, regarding Child protection;
d. capacity building of protection services for Women and Children;
e. guarantee of continuity of education in accordance with the 12 (twelve) year Compulsory Basic Education program; and
f. guarantee of obtaining basic health Services.
2. Fulfillment of social welfare of Women and Children for reducing vulnerability risks, includes:
a. identification and/or early detection of vulnerable Women and Children;
b. mediation and counseling for vulnerable Women and Children;
c. services and facilitation of support for vulnerable Women and Children; and d. care support for Children who need alternative care.
3. Fulfillment of social welfare of Women and Children for handling Victims, includes:
a. fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children who become Victims;
b. referral services;
c. rehabilitation; and d. reintegration.
4. Handling of Child Victims as referred to in paragraph (3) have the right to receive protection from local mass media coverage both electronic and print to ensure the future of the Child.

Article 28

1. Data and information as referred to in Article 27 become material for the formulation of policies, programs, budgets, monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of Women and Children against acts of Violence.
2. The formulation of policies, programs, budgets, monitoring and evaluation as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented with the mechanism of:
a. making mapping, long-term, medium-term and short-term plans;
b. making agreements on the periodization of monthly and annual work meetings;
c. making agreements on the collection, mapping and presentation of data between regional apparatus organizations;
d. incorporating agreements into programs and budgets; and
e. conducting scheduling of monitoring, evaluation and reporting.

Article 5

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. forms of Violence;
b. rights of Victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
e. coordination and cooperation;
f. Community and business participation;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. reporting; and
i. sources of funds.

Article 4

This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. respect and protect Human Rights;
b. guarantee the rights of every Woman and Child to survival, growth and development;
c. non-discrimination;
d. protect Women and Children from threats, fear, torture and or treatment that degrades the degree, self-esteem and dignity of humanity;
e. prevent forms of violence against Women and Children;
f. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against Women and Children;
g. protect and provide a sense of security for Women and Children;
h. provide services to Women and Children victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
i. protect and prevent all forms of discrimination against Women and Children in the region;
j. Women's Empowerment;
k. the best interests of the Child; and
l. realize a region that is suitable for Women and Children.

